       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't address either concern. You told me you're not a clinician, so you can't confirm the dose as the prescriber. The dose is also about double the maximum recommended daily amount of metformin, 5,100 mg per day against roughly 2,550 mg. That's a patient-safety risk, not just a formality.\n\nHere is what I'd suggest:\n- **Ask the prescriber to enter or confirm the order directly.** They can also tell me themselves if they want me to enter it.\n- **If it was a typo,** I can enter a standard dose once the prescriber gives me the correct one. One example is 850 mg three times daily with meals.\n- **If the high dose is truly intended,** the prescriber should document why. Pharmacy should review it before it's entered.\n\nI can enter the order as soon as a prescriber gives me a clinically verified dose."
